{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T17:41:09.822Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "conflicting-claims computes ancestry from the events present LOCALLY (reduce.cljc:168), and a replica's set is partial between syncs by definition. Confirmed: a strictly linear single-author history reports :conflicted when one unrelated intermediate event has not arrived, and explain tells the operator to supersede a conflict that does not exist. dag/missing-parents detects exactly this and is consulted in one place only (audit.clj:530, inside verify) - no derivation path, lens, explain or next asks whether the log it reasons over is complete. Convergence is a statement about the limit; every read happens before it. Derivation should carry a completeness qualifier and the lenses should surface it."} :event/parents #{"sha256-69161aec2ff48d3bc9e2adafff3607a68a2feaaf9712433eb8d36c33e5ffeadc"} :event/ticket #uuid "b7549f2f-a7de-4487-b5d3-374c69e6faef" :event/type :fact/assert}